    "narrative": "The Austin Waves are positioned for a high-ceiling outing today, headlined by **Luis Garc\u00eda Jr.**, whose 74.56 score makes him our premier start. He faces Burrows, an SP with a favorable 4.71 xERA, and benefits from a massive 17% SP skill adjustment and a 14% platoon edge. Similarly, **Jackson Merrill** (72.26) presents an elite profile for our strategy; beyond his solid matchup against Pfaadt, his ability to exploit the pitcher's slow delivery makes him a high-leverage target for stolen bases, a vital component for our 5x5 standing. **Kyle Tucker** and **Cole Carrigg** also offer strong floors against their respective left-handed matchups, as both benefit from favorable SP skill metrics that boost their production projections well into the 60s.\n\nThe most difficult bench decision involved balancing the volume of the Washington stack against the sub-60 projections of players like **Dominic Smith** (53.17) and **Heliot Ramos** (51.98). While **Heliot Ramos** holds a prime leadoff spot, the matchup against an elite arm like Gausman (3.71 xERA) suppressed his score, rendering him a marginal start. **Dominic Smith** barely cleared the 50-point threshold; he remains in the lineup purely due to a platoon advantage, but he is a candidate to be pulled if we prioritize high-probability plate appearances later in the slate. We continue to navigate the absence of core contributors like **Luis Robert Jr.**, **Jordan Westburg**, **Jacob Wilson**, and **Gunnar Henderson**, leaving us to lean heavily on the depth provided by **Curtis Mead**\u2014who is trending upward with a 63.58 score today\u2014and **Andy Pages** to carry the offensive load. \n\nRisks today are moderate, primarily stemming from **Heliot Ramos** facing the toughest pitcher on our slate and the potential for late-inning defensive substitutions if games get out of hand. We remain vigilant regarding the health of our bench depth, including **Jorge Polanco**, **Josh Lowe**, **Nolan Schanuel**, **Josh Jung**, **Coby Mayo**, **Miguel Vargas**, **Brayan Rocchio**, **Sam Antonacci**, **Wade Meckler**, **Liam Hicks**, and **Denzer Guzman**, who represent our next wave should injury or underperformance force a change in our roster construction. With the scarcity of steals in our current build, the emphasis on **Jackson Merrill** and **Nasim Nunez** to catalyze the base paths remains our primary strategic lever for this afternoon\u2019s action.",
